333
00:33:32,078 --> 00:33:36,836
比如在第四个表达式中，Python 就无法决定是进行加法还是拼接。
like in the fourth expression, Python can't decide whether to add or concatenate.

334
00:33:37,678 --> 00:33:41,156
在这种情况下，Python 会抛出一个类型错误。
In this case, Python throws a type error.

335
00:33:41,998 --> 00:33:48,356
这里的核心要点是，加号运算符的行为取决于两侧数据的类型。
The main takeaway here is that the plus operator's behavior depends on the types of data on either side.

336
00:33:49,166 --> 00:33:51,748
太棒了，让我们来完成第三个问题。
Awesome, let's finish up with problem three.

337
00:33:52,590 --> 00:33:59,588
在这个问题中，我们有三个错误的打印语句，我们的目标是修复这三个句子，让它们能正常运行且不报错。
In this problem, we're given three broken print statements, and our goal is to fix all three so they run without errors.

338
00:34:00,430 --> 00:34:06,180
从第一个打印语句开始，我们看到它使用单引号来包裹字符串。
Starting with the first print statement, we see it uses single quotes to wrap the strings.

339
00:34:07,022 --> 00:34:15,103
问题在于这个字符串包含一个撇号，也就是和单引号一样的字符，所以 Python 会把撇号读成
The problem is that the string contains an apostrophe, the same character as a single quote, so Python reads the apostrophe

340
00:34:15,264 --> 00:34:16,452
字符串的结束。
as the end of the string.

341
00:34:17,262 --> 00:34:23,620
为了解决这个问题，我们换成双引号，这样 Python 就不会被里面的撇号搞混了。
To fix this issue, we switch to double quotes, so Python doesn't get confused by the apostrophe inside.

342
00:34:24,429 --> 00:34:33,092
第二个字符串有相反的问题。这个字符串是用双引号创建的，但文本本身也包含双引号。
The second string has the opposite problem. The string is created with double quotes, but the text itself also contains double quotes.

343
00:34:33,934 --> 00:34:39,268
这意味着 Python 会把第一个内部的双引号视为结束引号。
This means that Python sees the first of those inner double quotes as the closing quote.

344
00:34:40,110 --> 00:34:44,068
为了修复这个错误，我们将外层的包裹换成单引号。
To fix this error, we swap the outer wrapping to single quotes.

345
00:34:44,909 --> 00:34:49,891
现在 Python 能正确地把字符串内部的引号当作普通字符处理了。
Now Python properly treats the quotes inside the string as regular characters.

346
00:34:50,734 --> 00:34:59,424
第三行试图拼接一个字符串和一个整数，这意味着我们遇到了在问题
The third line tries to concatenate a string and an integer, which means we have the same type mixing issue as we discussed in problem

347
00:34:59,744 --> 00:34:59,984
二中讨论过的同样的类型混合问题。
two.

348
00:35:00,750 --> 00:35:07,428
这里的解决方法是将运算符的两边都变成字符串，这样 Python 就能把它们拼接在一起了。
The fix here is to make both sides of the operator into strings so that Python can concatenate them together.

349
00:35:08,270 --> 00:35:12,836
运行这一行时，Python 会把两边连接起来而不会报错。
Running this line, Python joins the two sides together without an error.

350
00:35:13,904 --> 00:35:17,572
很好，这些就是我们三个练习题的解答。
Great, those are the solutions to our three practice problems.

351
00:35:18,864 --> 00:35:30,384
现在我们知道如何创建字符串并拼接文本了。但到目前为止，我们处理过的每一个值，无论是字符串、整数还是浮点数，都是用完就丢弃了。
Now we know how to create strings and join text together. But every value we've worked with so far, whether it was a string or an integer or a float, has been used once and then forgotten.

352
00:35:30,704 --> 00:35:35,664
在下一个部分，我们将学习如何存储数据，以便稍能在程序中调用。
In the next section, we'll learn how to store data so that we can use it later in our programs.

353
00:35:36,494 --> 00:35:48,704
你写出的几乎每一个 Python 程序都需要存储信息。比如用户名、运行中的总计，或者计算的结果。要在 Python 中做到这一点，你需要用到变量。
Almost every Python program you'll ever write needs to store information. A username, a running total, or the results of a calculation. To do this in Python, you'll need variables.

354
00:35:49,646 --> 00:35:53,668
为了理解它是如何运作的，你可以把变量想象成一个贴有标签的储藏罐。
To see how that works, think of a variable as a labeled storage jar.

355
00:35:54,542 --> 00:36:00,996
那个罐子的标签就像是变量名，而我们放进罐子里的任何东西就是变量的值。
That jar's label is like a variable name, and whatever we put inside the jar is the variable's value.

356
00:36:01,838 --> 00:36:09,060
看看这在 Python 中是怎么实现的，假设我们正在写一个程序，需要记住一个用户名以便稍后使用。
To see how this works in Python, suppose we're writing a program that needs to remember a username so we can use it later.

357
00:36:09,902 --> 00:36:14,180
为了创建一个用于用户名的变量，我们首先从写出变量名称开始。
To create a variable for the username, we start by writing the variable's name.

358
00:36:15,054 --> 00:36:22,244
最佳实践是选择一个能描述该变量存储内容的名称，所以我们用 username 这个名字。
It's best practice to pick a name that is descriptive of what the variable will store, so we'll go with the name username.

359
00:36:23,086 --> 00:36:26,692
创建变量名就像是给我们的储藏罐贴上标签。
Creating a variable name is like giving a label to our storage jar.

360
00:36:27,598 --> 00:36:31,024
在变量名称后面，我们写一个等号。
After the variable name, we write an equal sign.

361
00:36:32,304 --> 00:36:35,460
这个等号被称为赋值运算符。
The equal sign is called the assignment operator.

362
00:36:36,398 --> 00:36:41,988
它告诉 Python 把我们指定的右侧值，赋值给左边的变量名。
It tells Python to assign the value we'll specify on the right to the variable name on the left.

363
00:36:42,830 --> 00:36:47,344
最后，在等号后面，我们要写下想要存储的值。
Finally, after the equal sign, we write the value we want to store.

364
00:36:47,584 --> 00:36:49,744
在这个例子中，是字符串 summer。
In this case, the string summer.

365
00:36:50,606 --> 00:36:55,108
当代码运行时，字符串 summer 就会被放入我们的存储罐里。
The string summer is what gets put inside our storage jar when the code is run.

366
00:36:55,982 --> 00:36:58,660
太棒了！我们现在创建了第一个变量。
Awesome! We've now created our first variable.

367
00:36:59,502 --> 00:37:04,324
从现在开始，程序中的 username 变量就包含了字符串 summer。
From this point forward in our program, the variable username holds the string summer.

368
00:37:05,198 --> 00:37:11,716
这意味着在实际操作中，当我们写下 username 时，Python 会用字符串 summer 来代替。
This means that, in practice, when we write username, Python will substitute in the string summer.

369
00:37:12,558 --> 00:37:19,332
在 Jupyter notebook 中工作时，只要把变量写在单元格的最后一行，就能输出它的值。
When working in a Jupyter notebook, we can output the variable's value just by writing it on the last line of a cell.

370
00:37:20,238 --> 00:37:29,988
但要在普通的 Python 程序中，或者在 Jupyter notebook 非最后一行的位置输出变量值，我们需要使用 print 函数。
But to output a variable's value in a normal Python program, or anywhere in a Jupyter notebook that's not the final line of a cell, we need to use the print function.

371
00:37:30,830 --> 00:37:39,204
为了看看 print 函数如何与变量配合工作，我们可以在新单元格中调用 print 函数并传入 username 变量。
To see how the print function works with variables, in a new cell, we can call the print function and pass in the username variable.

372
00:37:40,110 --> 00:37:42,464
运行这个单元格，我们也得到了 summer。
Running the cell, we also get summer.

373
00:37:43,438 --> 00:37:49,700
注意看，Jupyter 的输出显示带引号的 summer，但 print 给出的却是没有引号的 summer。
Notice that the Jupyter output shows summer with quotes, but print gives us summer without them.

374
00:37:50,542 --> 00:37:57,348
这是因为 print 是为了人类阅读而格式化的，而不是原始的 Python 数据，所以去掉了引号。
That's because print formats the output for human reading, not raw Python, so the quotes get dropped.

375
00:37:58,224 --> 00:38:05,104
很好！除了存储用户名，我们可能还想存储用户的密码。1234。
Great! In addition to storing a username, we might also want to store the user's password. 1234.

376
00:38:06,030 --> 00:38:12,004
虽然这个密码是一个整数，但我们依然可以像存储 username 字符串一样把它存入变量中。
Even though this password is an integer, we can store it in a variable just like we store the username string.

377
00:38:12,846 --> 00:38:18,180
为了确认赋值成功，我们可以打印出该变量并运行单元格。
To confirm the assignment was successful, we can print the variable and run the cell.

378
00:38:19,022 --> 00:38:27,344
除了字符串和数字数据，变量还可以存储任何类型的数据，比如列表、布尔值、字典
In addition to strings and numeric data, variables can store any type of data lists, booleans, dictionaries,

379
00:38:27,584 --> 00:38:28,196
等等还有更多。
and more.

380
00:38:29,038 --> 00:38:34,468
如果你想了解更多关于这些数据类型的知识，我们在简介里放了相关视频的链接。
If you want to learn more about these data types, we left a link to our videos on these topics in the description.

381
00:38:35,310 --> 00:38:41,024
太棒了！现在你已经掌握了如何创建变量来存储值，并在程序后续使用它们。
Awesome! Now you understand how to create variables to store values and use them later in your program.

382
00:38:41,870 --> 00:38:47,492
但假设用户稍后想更新保存在 password 变量中的密码。
But suppose the user later wants to update their password stored in the password variable.

383
00:38:48,334 --> 00:38:57,572
我们可以在程序的任何地方更改变量的值。这被称为重新赋值，我们可以根据需要进行多次操作。
We can change a variable's value at any point in our program. This is called reassignment, and we can do it as many times as we'd like.

384
00:38:58,414 --> 00:39:05,700
要重新赋值 password 变量，我们写下它的名字，接着是赋值运算符和新值。
To reassign the password variable, we write its name, followed by the assignment operator and the new value.

385
00:39:06,542 --> 00:39:12,464
从这一刻起，password 变量现在包含的值就是 4567。
After this point, the password variable now contains the value 4567.

386
00:39:13,358 --> 00:39:22,532
但在这一刻之前，password 仍然是 1234。很好！现在我们知道如何存储和更新变量中的值了。
But before this point, password is still 1234. Great! Now we know how to store and update the values in our variables.

387
00:39:23,374 --> 00:39:32,388
到目前为止，我们关注的是变量里装了什么。但变量的命名也很重要，Python 对什么是有效的名称有相关规则。
So far we've focused on what variables hold. But variable names matter too, and Python has rules about what counts as a valid name.

388
00:39:33,230 --> 00:39:35,744
如果你违反了这些规则，你的代码就无法运行。
Break them, and your code won't run.

389
00:39:36,064 --> 00:39:41,988
为了看看这些规则是如何运作的，让我们创建一个存储用户最喜欢的三个甜点的新变量。
To see how these rules work, let's create a new variable that stores a user's three favorite desserts.

390
00:39:43,470 --> 00:39:47,610
你可能会认为一个自然的变量名应该是 three fave desserts。
You might think a natural variable name would be three fave desserts.

391
00:39:48,704 --> 00:39:51,556
但是当我们运行这段代码时，Python 会报错。
But when we run this, Python throws an error.

392
00:39:52,462 --> 00:39:55,588
这是因为变量名不能以数字开头。
This is because variable names can't start with a number.

393
00:39:56,494 --> 00:40:05,348
不过，变量名的其他部分可以使用数字，所以像 my threefave desserts 这样的变量名
However, numbers are allowed in all other parts of a variable name, so a variable name like my threefave desserts

394
00:40:05,744 --> 00:40:06,564
是可以运行的。
will work.

395
00:40:07,438 --> 00:40:09,024
好的，那没问题。
Okay, that's fine.

396
00:40:09,344 --> 00:40:13,284
但 my threefave desserts 并不好读。
But my threefave desserts isn't very easy to read.

397
00:40:14,126 --> 00:40:17,504
一个自然的解决方法是在单词之间加上空格。
A natural fix would be to add spaces between the words.

398
00:40:17,744 --> 00:40:20,580
但是运行这个单元格时，我们又得到了一个错误。
But running the cell, we get another error.

399
00:40:21,422 --> 00:40:24,996
这是因为 Python 不允许在变量名中使用空格。
That's because Python doesn't allow spaces in variable names.

400
00:40:25,998 --> 00:40:33,412
相反，为了让变量名更易读，Python 程序员经常使用下划线来代替空格。
Instead, to make variable names more readable, Python programmers often use underscore characters to represent spaces.

401
00:40:34,350 --> 00:40:36,868
现在我们运行这个单元格，它就可以正常工作了。
When we run the cell now, it works.

402
00:40:37,774 --> 00:40:42,788
最后还要记住的一条规则是，变量名是区分大小写的。
One final rule to keep in mind is that variable names are case sensitive.

403
00:40:43,630 --> 00:40:55,012
这意味着对于 Python 来说，my three fave desserts 和首字母大写的 My three favedesserts 是两个完全不同的变量。
This means that my three fave desserts and my three favedesserts with a capital M are two completely separate variables as far as Python is concerned.

404
00:40:55,854 --> 00:41:00,004
所以，在创建和使用变量时，保持一致非常重要。
So when creating and using variables, it's important to be consistent.

405
00:41:00,846 --> 00:41:04,144
太棒了！现在你知道如何将任何值存储在变量中了。
Awesome! Now you know how to store any value in a variable.

406
00:41:04,430 --> 00:41:09,668
可以在程序的任何地方使用它，在需要时更新它，并给它起个正确的名字。
Use it anywhere in your program, update it when needed, and name it correctly.

407
00:41:10,464 --> 00:41:19,104
现在让我们去描述栏里提供的练习笔记本，来积累一些操作变量的经验。如果你想自己尝试这些练习，可以到这里暂停视频。
Now let's head to the practice notebook linked in the description to get some experience working with variables. If you want to try these exercises on your own, pause the video here.

408
00:41:19,344 --> 00:41:23,664
然后在下一部分，我们将一起一步步讲解这些题目的答案。
Then in the next section, we'll walk through the solutions together step by step.

409
00:41:24,462 --> 00:41:26,596
好了，让我们进入第一个问题。
Alright, let's jump into problem one.

410
00:41:27,502 --> 00:41:33,284
在这个问题中，我们创建两个变量，然后打印出一个同时包含这两个变量的句子。
In this problem, we create two variables and then print a single sentence that uses both of them.

411
00:41:34,094 --> 00:41:39,972
我们需要一个名为 plant_name 的字符串变量，以及一个名为 watering_days 的整数变量。
We'll need a string variable called plant name and an integer variable called watering days.

412
00:41:40,814 --> 00:41:50,244
为了存储植物名称，我们写下变量名 plant_name，接着是赋值运算符，然后在引号中放入植物的名称。
To store the plant name, we write the variable plant name and the assignment operator and the name of the plant in between quotes.

413
00:41:51,104 --> 00:41:59,584
同样地，对于两次浇水之间的天数，我们写下变量名 watering_days，然后是赋值运算符，
Similarly, for the number of days between waterings, we write the variable name, watering days, the assignment operator,

414
00:42:00,144 --> 00:42:03,972
再写一个代表两次浇水之间天数的整数。
and a whole number to represent the number of days between waterings.

415
00:42:04,814 --> 00:42:13,636
为了打印包含这两个信息的单行内容，我们调用 Print 函数，并将句子文本和变量作为独立的参数传入。
To print one line that mentions both, we call print and pass in the sentence text and variables as separate arguments.

416
00:42:18,574 --> 00:42:25,284
当我们运行这个单元格时，我们就能看到填入植物名称和浇水计划的句子了。
When we run the cell, we see our sentence with the plant name and the watering schedule filled in.

417
00:42:26,126 --> 00:42:32,484
很好！在第二个问题中，我们将练习在初始赋值后更新变量的值。
Great! For problem two, we'll practice updating a variable's value after it's initially assigned.

418
00:42:33,326 --> 00:42:41,764
在这个问题中，我们将使用一个名为 water_ounces 的变量来记录龟背竹的浇水日志，以此追踪浇水壶里有多少盎司的水。
In this problem, we'll keep a watering log for the Monstera using a variable called water ounces to track how many ounces are in the watering can.

419
00:42:42,638 --> 00:42:55,748
我们从 64 盎司开始，打印这个数值，然后减去我们用来给植物浇水的水量。再次 Print，然后加上我们从水龙头里加满的水量，最后再 Print 一次。
We'll start with 64 ounces, print the amount, and subtract what we use to water the plant. Print again, and then add back what we refill from the tap, and print one last time.

420
00:42:56,622 --> 00:43:05,744
关键点在于，每当数量发生变化时，我们都会使用右侧当前的 water_ounces 值来重新给 water_ounces 赋值，
The important part is that each time the amount changes, we reassign water ounces using the current value of water ounces on the right side,

421
00:43:05,984 --> 00:43:08,356
不是我们在旁边计算出的总数。
not a total we calculated off to the side.

422
00:43:09,198 --> 00:43:12,484
我们首先将 64 赋值给 water ounces。
We begin by assigning 64 to water ounces.

423
00:43:13,294 --> 00:43:16,548
为了记录初始数量，我们 Print 出 water ounces。
To log the starting amount, we print water ounces.

424
00:43:17,390 --> 00:43:20,224
运行单元格后，我们看到 64。
Running the cell, we see 64.

425
00:43:21,104 --> 00:43:21,744
接下来，
Next,

426
00:43:23,054 --> 00:43:26,372
我们给龟背竹浇水，使用了 20 盎司。
we water the Monstera and use 20 ounces.

427
00:43:27,214 --> 00:43:33,828
为了从现有水量中扣除这部分，我们将 water ounces 重新赋值为 water ounces 减去 20。
To pull that out of what we already have, we reassign water ounces to water ounces minus 20.

428
00:43:34,670 --> 00:43:38,404
我们可以通过再次 Print water ounces 来查看更新后的总数。
We can see the updated total by printing water ounces again.

429
00:43:39,246 --> 00:43:46,340
运行单元格后，第二个数字是 44，这意味着我们的 water ounces 变量已成功更新。
Running the cell, the second number is 44, which means our water ounces variable was successfully updated.

430
00:43:47,182 --> 00:43:52,804
之后，我们从水龙头接水，并补回 32 盎司。
After that, we refill the can from the tab and add 32 ounces back.

431
00:43:53,678 --> 00:44:00,196
我们再次重新赋值 water ounces，这次是将当前 water ounces 中的数值加上 32。
We reassign water ounces again, this time adding 32 to whatever is currently in water ounces.

432
00:44:01,070 --> 00:44:05,508
为了查看更新后的水量，我们再 Print 一次 water ounces。
To see the updated amount of water, we print water ounces one more time.

433
00:44:06,350 --> 00:44:09,904
运行单元格后，第三行显示为 76。
Running the cell, the third line shows 76.

434
00:44:10,958 --> 00:44:17,796
太棒了！每当数据发生变化且我们需要追踪最新值时，像这样重新赋值变量是非常常见的做法。
Awesome! Reassigning variables like this is common whenever data changes and we need to keep track of the latest value.

435
00:44:18,670 --> 00:44:20,420
让我们来完成第三个问题。
Let's finish with problem three.

436
00:44:21,294 --> 00:44:27,300
在这个问题中，给出的代码无法运行，因为变量名称违反了 Python 的命名规则。
In this problem, we're given code that won't run because the variable names break Python's naming rules.

437
00:44:28,142 --> 00:44:35,844
我们通过在名称中添加下划线来修正这些名称，并确保名称不会以数字开头，也不会包含空格。
We'll fix the names by adding underscores to the names, and we'll make sure we don't start a name with a digit or put a space inside it.

438
00:44:36,718 --> 00:44:42,852
第一个无效名称 second_underscore_plant 以数字开头，这是 Python 不允许的。
The first invalid name, second underscore plant, starts with a number, which Python doesn't allow.

439
00:44:43,726 --> 00:44:51,172
为了修复这个问题，我们将数字替换为单词 second，这样在保留原意的同时去掉了开头的数字。
To fix this, we replace the number with the word, second, which keeps the same idea without the leading digit.

440
00:44:52,014 --> 00:45:00,388
另一个变量名称 plant space type 试图使用空格，Python 会将其识别为两个独立的词，而不是一个标识符。
The other variable name, plant space type, tries to use a space, which Python reads as two separate words instead of one identifier.

441
00:45:01,230 --> 00:45:05,220
为了解决这个问题，我们只需在单词之间添加一个下划线。
To fix this issue, we simply add an underscore between the words.

442
00:45:06,062 --> 00:45:10,340
最后，我们更新 Print 调用，使其使用新的变量名称。
Finally, we update the print call so it uses the new variable names.

443
00:45:12,814 --> 00:45:20,708
当我们运行单元格时，看到 cactus 和 succulent 被打印在同一行，中间用空格隔开，且代码顺利运行。
When we run the cell, we see cactus and succulent printed on one line, separated by a space, and the code runs cleanly.

444
00:45:21,550 --> 00:45:24,804
很好，这些就是三个练习题的解答。
Great, those are the solutions to all three practice problems.

445
00:45:25,824 --> 00:45:30,384
现在我们知道如何将值存储在变量中，并在程序稍后重复使用它们了。
Now we know how to store values in variables and reuse them later in our program.

446
00:45:30,704 --> 00:45:37,744
但是每当我们在一句句子中 Print 一个变量时，我们都必须用逗号来分隔单词和变量名称。
But every time we printed a variable inside of a sentence, we had to separate the words and the variable names with commas.

447
00:45:38,224 --> 00:45:44,064
在下一个部分，我们将学习一种更好的方法，直接将变量名称嵌入到字符串中。
In the next section, we'll learn a better way to directly embed variable names inside of strings.

448
00:45:44,784 --> 00:45:47,104
为什么这个字符串前面有一个 f？
Why is there an f before this string?

449
00:45:47,264 --> 00:45:49,476
还有这些括号是怎么回事？
And what's going on with the brackets?

450
00:45:50,318 --> 00:45:54,788
在 Python 中，这种语法创建了一个格式化字符串，简称 F string。
In Python, this syntax creates a formatted string, or f string for short.

451
00:45:55,310 --> 00:46:00,996
到本段视频结束时，你就会掌握如何使用 F strings 格式化文本并让输出结果更易于阅读。
By the end of this video, you'll know how to format text with f strings and make your outputs easier to read.

452
00:46:02,190 --> 00:46:08,784
为了熟悉 F string 的语法，让我们写一个简单的程序来显示分配给变量 ftemp 的温度。
To get familiar with the f string syntax, let's write a simple program to display the temperature assigned to the variable ftemp.

453
00:46:10,254 --> 00:46:16,644
具体来说，我们的程序应该生成一段文字，内容是：温度为 67 华氏度。
Specifically, our program should generate a string that reads, the temperature is 67 degrees Fahrenheit.

454
00:46:17,710 --> 00:46:24,900
但为了灵活性，我们不想在字符串中硬编码数值 67，以防 ftemp 变量发生变化。
But for flexibility, we don't want to hard code the value 67 in the string in case the f temp variable changes.

455
00:46:25,902 --> 00:46:30,532
相反，我们希望直接将 ftemp 的值嵌入到字符串中。
Instead, we'd like to embed the value of ftp directly in the string.

456
00:46:31,374 --> 00:46:33,508
使用 F string 可以轻松实现这一点。
This is easy to do with an f string.

457
00:46:34,574 --> 00:46:41,284
我们只需在第一个引号前加上 f，就能把这个普通字符串转换成 F string。
We can convert this regular string into an f string by simply writing f before the first quotation mark.

458
00:46:42,126 --> 00:46:48,932
现在有了 F string，我们可以通过在花括号中写入变量名称来插入 ftemp 的值。
Now that we have an f string, we can insert the value of ftp by writing the variable's name between curly braces.

459
00:46:49,838 --> 00:46:56,484
这种语法会告诉 Python 插入 f temp 的值，而不是字面上的字符串 f_temp。
This syntax tells Python to insert the value of f temp and not the literal string f underscore temp.

460
00:46:57,486 --> 00:47:05,252
运行单元格后，我们可以看到 F string 里的 f temp 变量确实被替换成了它的值，即 67。
Running the cell, we can see that the f temp variable inside the f string was indeed replaced by its value, 60 sep.

461
00:47:06,126 --> 00:47:10,852
这本身已经很有用了，但 F string 能让我们做更多事情。
This is already useful on its own, but f string allows us to do much more.

462
00:47:11,854 --> 00:47:16,388
特别是，我们可以在花括号中显示任何表达式的结果。
In particular, we can display the result of any expression between the braces.

463
00:47:17,264 --> 00:47:23,204
例如，假设我们希望程序报告的温度是摄氏度而不是华氏度。
For example, suppose we want our program to report the temperature in Celsius instead of Fahrenheit.

464
00:47:24,110 --> 00:47:33,412
我们可以直接在 F string 中进行转换：用 f temp 减去 32，然后除以 1.8。
We can do the conversion from Fahrenheit to Celsius directly inside the F string by subtracting 32 from F temp and dividing by 1.8.

465
00:47:34,382 --> 00:47:41,540
当这行代码执行时，Python 会先计算转换表达式，然后再将结果插入到字符串中。
When this line is executed, Python first evaluates the conversion expression and then inserts the result in the string.

466
00:47:42,542 --> 00:47:50,500
运行单元格后，我们得到的结果是温度为 19.4444443 摄氏度。
Running the cell, we get that the temperature is 19.4444443 degrees Celsius.

467
00:47:51,438 --> 00:47:55,172
好的，这虽然解决了问题，但小数点后的位数太多了。
Okay, that did the job, but that's way too many decimals.

468
00:47:56,206 --> 00:48:02,148
我们应该通过将温度保留一位或两位小数来优化输出格式。
We should probably improve the format of the output by rounding the temperature to one or two decimal places.

469
00:48:03,150 --> 00:48:06,756
幸运的是，使用 F strings，对数字进行舍入非常简单。
Luckily, with F strings, rounding numbers is easy.

470
00:48:07,822 --> 00:48:12,932
每当我们想要格式化括号中的表达式时，首先在后面写一个冒号。
Anytime we want to format the expression between brackets, we start by writing a colon.

471
00:48:13,902 --> 00:48:18,308
从这里开始，我们有很多选项来自定义结果的显示方式。
From here, we have a lot of options to customize how our result is displayed.

472
00:48:19,246 --> 00:48:29,636
为了格式化表达式中的小数位，我们写一个点，接着是我们要显示的位数（比如 1），然后用字母 F 表示将结果作为浮点数显示。
To format the decimal places in the expression, we write a period, the number of decimal places we want to display, one, and the letter F to display the result as a float.

473
00:48:30,734 --> 00:48:34,628
运行单元格后，我们得到了保留一位小数的摄氏度数值。
Running the cell, we get a Celsius value rounded to one decimal place.

474
00:48:35,598 --> 00:48:40,420
如果我们想保留两位小数，只需把 1 换成 2。
If we wanted to round two decimal places, we'd just replace the one with a two.

475
00:48:42,414 --> 00:48:48,228
这没问题，但你可能会好奇，为什么要在位数后面写一个 f？
This works fine, but you might be wondering, why do we need to write the f after the number of places?

476
00:48:49,166 --> 00:48:55,364
嗯，这是因为 F string 提供多种显示小数的方法，而浮点数只是其中一种选择。
Well, it's because f strings offer multiple ways to display decimal numbers, and floats are just one option.

477
00:48:56,366 --> 00:49:02,544
例如，我们可以用 e 代替 f，将结果以科学计数法显示。
For example, we could instead display the results in scientific notation by replacing f with e.

478
00:49:04,046 --> 00:49:07,972
或者我们也可以使用百分号将数值格式化为百分比。
Or we could format the value as a percentage using a percent sign.

479
00:49:09,486 --> 00:49:16,068
但既然我们处理的是温度，将数值格式化为浮点数最合理，所以我们继续用 F。
But since we're working with temperatures, formatting the value as a float makes the most sense, so we'll stick with F.

480
00:49:16,910 --> 00:49:17,504
太棒了！
Great!

481
00:49:17,744 --> 00:49:23,556
正如我们之前看到的，F strings 可以让我们灵活地控制小数如何显示。
As we've seen so far, F strings give us the flexibility to format how decimal numbers are displayed.

482
00:49:24,622 --> 00:49:26,692
但 F strings 功能更强大。
But F strings can do more.

483
00:49:27,694 --> 00:49:31,908
特别是，我们还可以用它们让大数字更容易阅读。
In particular, we can also use them to make big numbers easier to read.

484
00:49:32,942 --> 00:49:42,116
为了看看这是如何实现的，让我们来表示太阳核心的温度，即 2700 万华氏度，并相应地更新变量名称。
To see how this works, let's represent the temperature at the sun's core, which is 27 million degrees Fahrenheit, and update the variable name accordingly.

485
00:49:43,022 --> 00:49:50,116
当我们运行这个单元格时，很难一眼看出结果是接近 1.5 亿还是只有 1500 万。
When we run the cell, it's hard to tell at a glance whether the result is almost 150 million or just 15 million.

486
00:49:50,958 --> 00:49:53,664
我们得手动去数位数才能确定。
We'd have to count the places manually to be

487
00:49:53,664 --> 00:50:01,380
为了提高这类大数字的可读性，F strings 允许我们添加逗号作为千位分隔符。
sure. To improve the readability of large numbers like this, f-strings allow us to add commas as thousands separators.

488
00:50:02,382 --> 00:50:05,988
要添加这些分隔符，我们只需在小数点前写一个逗号。
To add the separators, we simply write a comma before the period.

489
00:50:06,958 --> 00:50:10,820
当我们运行这个单元格时，我们的摄氏度数值现在有了逗号分隔符。
When we run the cell, our Celsius value now has comma separators.

490
00:50:11,822 --> 00:50:12,900
清晰多了。
Much clearer.

491
00:50:13,838 --> 00:50:20,804
到目前为止，我们已经利用 F string 通过舍入和逗号分隔符来提高表达式结果的可读性。
So far, we've used F string to improve the readability of an expression's result with rounding and comma separators.

492
00:50:21,646 --> 00:50:29,796
但当我们需要控制表达式周围的间距、对齐和填充时，F strings 还提供更多的自定义选项。
But F strings offer even more customization for situations where we want to control the spacing, alignment, and padding around our expression.

493
00:50:30,766 --> 00:50:39,268
例如，假设我们希望程序同时显示太阳核心的温度和地球表面的平均华氏度。
For example, let's say we want our program to display both the temperature at the core of the sun and the average temperature in Fahrenheit on Earth's surface.

494
00:50:40,270 --> 00:50:44,260
为了将这个值转换为摄氏度并显示出来，我们将使用另一个 F string。
To convert this value to Celsius and display it, we'll use another F string.

495
00:50:45,230 --> 00:50:50,020
因为我们想同时显示这两个字符串，所以我们会把它们放入打印语句中。
Since we want to display both strings at the same time, we'll pass them into print statements.

496
00:50:51,022 --> 00:50:54,500
当我们运行这个单元格时，我们得到了预期的两个温度。
When we run the cell, we get both temperatures as expected.

497
00:50:55,502 --> 00:51:00,452
但这些字符串的布局有点乱，因为结果占据的空间不同。
But the layout of these strings is a bit messy, since the results take up different amounts of space.

498
00:51:01,422 --> 00:51:08,644
为了解决这个问题，F-strings 让我们可以通过在小数位选项前写一个数字来控制结果占用的空间。
To fix that, F-strings let us control the space that a result will take up by writing a number in front of the decimal options.

499
00:51:09,486 --> 00:51:16,132
在我们的例子中，我们指定 15，以确保每个结果正好占用 15 个字符。
In our example, let's specify 15 to make sure each result takes up exactly 15 characters.

500
00:51:17,134 --> 00:51:22,084
当我们运行这个单元格时，每个结果都在一个宽度为 15 个字符的空间内显示。
When we run the cell, each result is displayed in a space that is 15 characters wide.

501
00:51:22,926 --> 00:51:28,260
由于两个数字都没有达到 15 个字符长，Python 会将结果推到最右侧。
Since neither number is 15 characters long, Python pushes the result all the way to the right.

502
00:51:29,422 --> 00:51:35,300
这没问题，但我们可以通过在冒号后添加对齐符号来更改结果的对齐方式。
That works fine, but we can change the alignment of our results by adding an alignment symbol after the colon.

503
00:51:36,302 --> 00:51:40,672
要让数值左对齐，我们在冒号后面紧接着加上小于号。
To left align the values, we add the less than symbol right after the colon.

504
00:51:41,678 --> 00:51:47,204
当我们再次运行这个单元格时，我们会看到数字现在被推到左侧，正如我们预期的那样。
When we run the cell again, we'll see the numbers are now pushed to the left, just as we expected.

505
00:51:48,206 --> 00:51:53,412
或者如果我们想让数值居中显示在 15 个字符中，我们可以使用尖角符号。
Or if we want the values to sit in the center of the 15 characters, we can use the caret.

506
00:51:54,990 --> 00:52:01,124
现在，你可能已经注意到当值没有占据全部宽度时，有些东西会填补额外的空间。
Now, you might have noticed when the value doesn't take up the full width, something fills in the extra space.

507
00:52:02,126 --> 00:52:05,732
默认情况下，这些剩余的位置是用空格字符填充的。
By default, those leftover spots are filled with space characters.

508
00:52:06,798 --> 00:52:08,912
但我们并不局限于使用空格。
But we're not limited to spaces.

509
00:52:09,166 --> 00:52:11,300
我们可以选择其他的字符。
We can choose a different character instead.

510
00:52:12,334 --> 00:52:16,772
我们可以通过在对齐符号前写下我们想要使用的字符来实现这一点。
We can do this by writing the character we want to use before the alignment symbol.

511
00:52:17,774 --> 00:52:23,460
例如，为了让结果更醒目，我们可以用星号来代替空格。
For example, to make the result stand out more, we can fill the space with asterisks instead.

512
00:52:24,430 --> 00:52:25,152
太棒了！
Awesome!

513
00:52:25,518 --> 00:52:29,380
正如你所看到的，F strings 有很多格式化选项。
As you've seen, there are a lot of options for formatting F strings.

514
00:52:30,112 --> 00:52:41,312
现在我们可以直接把数值放入句子中，并精确控制它们的显示方式。但到目前为止，我们还无法根据程序中的数值（比如温度）来显示不同的句子。
Now we can drop values straight into sentences and control exactly how they're displayed. But so far we can't show different sentences depending on the values in our programs, like the temperature.

515
00:52:41,552 --> 00:52:52,432
在下一节中，我们将学习如何根据不同的决策标准让程序走向不同的路径。你每天使用的应用都在不断做出决策。
In the next section, we'll learn how to direct our program down different paths based on different decision criteria. The apps you use every day constantly make decisions.

516
00:52:53,134 --> 00:52:57,668
这封邮件是垃圾邮件吗？现在够晚到可以切换到深色模式了吗？
Is this email spam? Is it late enough to switch to dark mode?

517
00:52:58,574 --> 00:53:01,092
电池电量低到需要显示警告了吗？
Is the battery low enough to show a warning?

518
00:53:02,030 --> 00:53:05,636
这些问题中的每一个都可以用简单的“是”或“否”来回答。
Each of these questions can be answered with a simple yes or no.

519
00:53:06,542 --> 00:53:11,364
让我们看看如何让我们的 Python 程序做出同样类型的决策。
Let's see how we can teach our Python programs to make the same kinds of decisions.

520
00:53:12,206 --> 00:53:16,932
假设我们想建立一个根据温度推荐穿衣建议的程序。
Suppose we want to build a program that recommends what to wear based on the temperature.

521
00:53:17,774 --> 00:53:23,044
如果温度低于华氏 50 度，建议是穿上外套。
If the temperature is below 50 degrees Fahrenheit, the recommendation is to wear a jacket.

522
00:53:23,886 --> 00:53:28,388
如果温度在 50 度或更高，建议就是不穿外套。
If the temperature is 50 or higher, the recommendation is to not wear a jacket.

523
00:53:29,230 --> 00:53:33,924
要编写做出这类决策的代码，我们需要两个基本要素。
To write the code that makes decisions like this, we need two basic ingredients.

524
00:53:34,766 --> 00:53:39,492
首先，我们需要一种方法来提出“是”或“否”的问题并表示它的答案。
First, we need a way to ask a yes or no question and represent its answer.

525
00:53:40,352 --> 00:53:44,452
其次，我们需要一种根据答案来运行不同代码的方法。
Second, we need a way to run different code based on the answer.

526
00:53:45,358 --> 00:53:47,972
让我们先来看看第一个要素。
Let's start by looking at the first ingredient.

527
00:53:48,910 --> 00:53:55,332
在 Python 中，对“是”或“否”问题的回答是用一种叫做布尔值的数据类型来表示的。
In Python, the answer to a yes or no question is represented using a data type called a Boolean.

528
00:53:56,270 --> 00:54:01,252
布尔值只能有两个值中的一个：true 或 false。
A Boolean can only have one of two values, true or false.

529
00:54:02,094 --> 00:54:05,828
例如，让我们创建一个名为 is_cold 的变量。
For example, let's create a variable called is cold.

530
00:54:06,670 --> 00:54:11,940
为了表示对“外面冷吗？”这个问题的“是”的回答，我们可以将其设为 true。
To represent a yes answer to the question, is it cold outside? we can set it to true.

531
00:54:12,782 --> 00:54:17,028
为了表示“否”的回答，我们会将 is_cold 设置为 false。
To represent a no answer, we would set is cold to false.

532
00:54:17,952 --> 00:54:20,996
行，但这种方法有一个问题。
Fine, but there's a problem with this approach.

533
00:54:21,966 --> 00:54:28,452
我们必须自己决定是否寒冷，然后手动输入 true 或 false。
We had to decide for ourselves whether it's cold, and then manually type in true or false.

534
00:54:29,294 --> 00:54:34,660
如果我们有实际的温度，并且想让 Python 来判断是否寒冷呢？
What if we have the actual temperature and we want Python to determine whether it's cold?

535
00:54:35,520 --> 00:54:42,244
例如，假设当前温度是 45，任何低于 50 的都算作寒冷。
For example, let's say the current temperature is 45, and anything below 50 counts as cold.

536
00:54:43,086 --> 00:54:50,724
为了问 Python“当前温度是否小于 50？”，我们写 temperature 小于号 50。
To ask Python, is the current temperature less than 50? We write temperature less than sign 50.

537
00:54:51,566 --> 00:54:56,196
当我们运行这个单元格时，Python 会计算这个表达式并输出 true。
When we run the cell, Python evaluates this expression and outputs true.

538
00:54:57,038 --> 00:55:00,580
这意味着，是的，温度低于 50。
This means that, yes, the temperature is below 50.

539
00:55:01,422 --> 00:55:07,044
如果我们改为将温度设为 55 并再次评估相同的条件，
If we instead change the temperature to 55 and evaluate the same condition again,

540
00:55:07,886 --> 00:55:12,900
Python 现在会产生 false，意味着温度不低于 50。
Python now produces false, meaning the temperature is not below 50.

541
00:55:13,742 --> 00:55:17,680
这个小于号被称为比较运算符。
This less than sign is called a comparison operator.

542
00:55:18,542 --> 00:55:25,572
它比较两个值并返回一个布尔值。如果关系成立就返回 True，否则返回 False。
It compares two values and gives us back a Boolean. True if the relationship holds, false if it doesn't.

543
00:55:26,446 --> 00:55:33,060
执行比较并查看结果很有用，但如果我们想在代码的后续部分使用这个结果呢？
Running a comparison and seeing the result is useful, but what if we want to use that answer later in our code?

544
00:55:33,998 --> 00:55:37,924
好的，我们可以像存储任何其他值一样，把它存进一个变量里。
Well, we can store it in a variable just like any other value.

545
00:55:38,800 --> 00:55:45,828
例如，我们将“温度小于 50”的结果赋值给一个名为 iscold 的变量。
For example, let's assign the result of temperature less than 50 to a variable called iscold.

546
00:55:46,670 --> 00:55:49,988
当 Python 执行这一行时，它是从右到左执行的。
When Python runs this line, it works from right to left.

547
00:55:50,894 --> 00:55:54,500
首先，它计算比较结果并得到 false。
First, it evaluates the comparison and gets false.

548
00:55:55,374 --> 00:55:58,532
然后它把这个布尔值存入 iscold 中。
Then it stores that Boolean in iscold.

549
00:55:59,374 --> 00:56:07,140
如果这种从右到左的顺序让人困惑，我们可以给比较部分加上括号，让计算顺序更清晰。
If this right to left order feels unclear, we can add parentheses around the comparison to make the evaluation order more obvious.

550
00:56:08,942 --> 00:56:14,020
小于运算符只是 Python 提供给我们的几种比较运算符之一。
The less than operator is just one of several comparison operators Python gives us.

551
00:56:14,830 --> 00:56:22,960
我们可以检查一个值是否大于、小于、等于、大于或等于、
We can check if a value is greater than, less than or equal to, greater than or equal to, equal to,

552
00:56:23,200 --> 00:56:25,348
或者不等于另一个值。
or not equal to another value.

553
00:56:26,190 --> 00:56:32,164
有一点需要注意，当我们要判断两个值是否相等时，我们使用双等号。
One thing to watch out for, when checking if two values are equal, we use a double equal sign.

554
00:56:33,006 --> 00:56:37,860
这与单等号不同，单等号是专门用于变量赋值的。
This is different from the single equal sign, which is reserved for variable assignment.

555
00:56:38,702 --> 00:56:47,300
太棒了，现在我们的工具箱里有了布尔值和比较运算符，这意味着我们可以提出问题并得到 true 或 false 的答案。
Great, so now we have Booleans and comparison operators in our toolkit, which means we can ask questions and get true or false answers.

556
00:56:48,142 --> 00:56:51,492
但目前，我们的程序只是知道了答案。
But right now, our program just knows the answer.

557
00:56:52,366 --> 00:56:55,556
它并没有根据这个结果去做任何实际的操作。
It doesn't actually do anything based on it.

558
00:56:56,462 --> 00:57:02,692
这就是第二个要素派上用场的地方。我们需要一种方法告诉 Python：如果这是真的，就执行这个操作。
That's where the second ingredient comes in. We need a way to tell Python, if this is true, then do this.

559
00:57:03,534 --> 00:57:06,084
让我们让 isCold 变量发挥作用。
Let's put our isCold variable to work.

560
00:57:06,926 --> 00:57:12,484
假设我们希望程序在 isCold 为 true 的情况下才打印“穿上外套”。
Say we want our program to print wear a jacket, but only if isCold is true.

561
00:57:13,326 --> 00:57:16,196
在 Python 中，我们通过 if 语句来实现这一点。
In Python, we do this with an if statement.

562
00:57:17,038 --> 00:57:20,240
if 语句的头部以关键字 if 开始。
The header of an if statement starts with the keyword if.

563
00:57:21,262 --> 00:57:26,560
这个关键字后面跟着一个条件。这里是 is cold，并以冒号结尾。
This keyword is followed by a condition. Here, is cold and ends with a colon.

564
00:57:27,502 --> 00:57:35,360
在下一行，通过缩进，我们写下当条件为真时应该发生的事情。在这种情况下，就是打印 wear a jacket。
On the next line, indented, we write what should happen when the condition is true. In this case, printing wear a jacket.

565
00:57:36,238 --> 00:57:43,844
那个缩进不仅仅是为了可读性。它是在告诉 Python，这一行属于 if 块的一部分。
That indentation isn't just for readability. It signals to Python that this line is part of the if block.

566
00:57:44,686 --> 00:57:52,676
为了看到区别，我们可以在 if 块之外添加一个不带缩进的行，来标记程序的结束。
To see the difference, let's add an unindented line outside of the if block to mark when the program finishes.

567
00:57:53,518 --> 00:57:57,280
无论 iscold 的值是多少，这一行都会执行。
This line will run regardless of the value of iscold.

568
00:57:58,158 --> 00:58:01,572
太棒了！现在让我们看看这个 if 语句的效果。
Great! Now let's see this if statement in action.

569
00:58:02,414 --> 00:58:09,360
当温度设置为 48 时，我们运行代码，会先得到 wear a jacket，接着是 end of program。
With the temperature set to 48, we run the code and get wear a jacket followed by end of program.

570
00:58:10,414 --> 00:58:18,020
原因如下：48 小于 50，所以比较返回 true，然后这个值被赋值给 isCold。
Here's why. 48 is less than 50, so the comparison returns true, which is then assigned to isCold.

571
00:58:18,862 --> 00:58:24,292
当 Python 到达 if 语句时，它首先会检查 isCold 是真还是假。
When Python reaches the if statement, it first checks whether isCold is true or false.

572
00:58:25,134 --> 00:58:31,460
在这种情况下，isCold 是真的。所以 Python 会运行缩进代码并输出 wear a jacket。
In this case, isCold is true. So Python runs the indented code and outputs where a jacket.

573
00:58:32,334 --> 00:58:38,276
在 if 块之后，Python 会继续执行非缩进代码，并输出 end of program。
After the if block, Python moves on to the unindented code and outputs end of program.

574
00:58:39,118 --> 00:58:44,068
很好，但假设天气变暖了，现在的温度是 55 度。
Great, but suppose it warms up and the temperature is now 55 degrees.

575
00:58:44,928 --> 00:58:49,088
现在当我们运行代码时，只会看到 end of program。
Now when we run the code, we only get end of program.

576
00:58:49,968 --> 00:58:55,844
这是因为 55 不低于 50，所以 isCold 被设为了假。
This is because 55 is not below 50, so isCold was set to false.

577
00:58:56,688 --> 00:59:02,436
然后，就像之前一样，Python 评估了条件，但这次结果是假的。
Then, like before, Python evaluated the condition, but this time it was false.

578
00:59:03,278 --> 00:59:08,388
所以 Python 完全跳过了缩进块，并继续执行非缩进代码。
So Python skipped the indented block entirely and moved on to the unindented code.

579
00:59:09,262 --> 00:59:15,460
太棒了！if 语句给了我们一条决策路径。如果条件为真，就运行这段代码。
Great! An if statement gives us one decision path. If the condition is true, run this code.

580
00:59:16,302 --> 00:59:22,596
但在很多情况下，我们也希望程序在条件为假时执行某些操作。
But in many cases, we also want our program to do something only when the condition is false.

581
00:59:23,534 --> 00:59:28,388
在我们的例子中，如果条件为假，我们想提示 no jacket。
In our example, we want to suggest no jacket if the condition is false.

582
00:59:29,262 --> 00:59:32,608
为了做到这一点，我们需要另一个关键字：else。
To do this, we'll need another keyword, else.

583
00:59:33,614 --> 00:59:41,252
要添加一个 else 块，我们在与 if 同一缩进层级写下关键字 else，后面加上冒号。
To add an else block, we'll write the keyword else at the same indentation level as the if followed by a colon.

584
00:59:42,094 --> 00:59:48,164
与 if 语句不同，else 语句不需要条件。它是备选方案。
Unlike the if statement, the else statement doesn't require a condition. It is the fallback option.

585
00:59:49,006 --> 00:59:53,508
在下一行，我们缩进那些我们希望在条件为假时运行的代码。
On the next line, we indent the code we want to run when the condition is false.

586
00:59:54,446 --> 00:59:57,380
在这种情况下，我们将打印 no jacket needed。
In this case, we'll print no jacket needed.

587
00:59:58,318 --> 01:00:01,028
太棒了，让我们看看这个 else 块的效果。
Awesome, let's see this else block in action.

588
01:00:01,934 --> 01:00:07,940
因为目前的温度设为 55，当我们运行代码时，is_cold 将是假的。
Since the temperature is currently set to 55, when we run the code, is cold will be false.

589
01:00:08,750 --> 01:00:13,028
这意味着 Python 将跳过 if 块，转而执行 else 块。
This means Python will skip the if block and run the else block instead.

590
01:00:13,902 --> 01:00:20,740
运行这个单元格，我们看到 no jacket needed，接着是 end of program，完全符合预期。
Running the cell, we see no jacket needed, followed by end of program, exactly as expected.

591
01:00:21,614 --> 01:00:26,928
如果温度降回到 45 度，isCold 将会是
And if the temperature falls back down to 45 degrees, isCold will be

592
01:00:26,928 --> 01:00:33,568
真的。这意味着 Python 会像我们之前看到的那样运行 if 块并打印 wear a jacket。
true. This means Python will run the if block just like we saw earlier and print wear a jacket.

593
01:00:34,542 --> 01:00:39,460
这次 else 块会被跳过，因为 if 条件得到了满足。
The else block will get skipped this time, because the if condition is satisfied.

594
01:00:40,302 --> 01:00:45,648
然后 Python 将继续执行非缩进代码并打印 end of program。
Then Python will continue on to the unindented code and print end of program.

595
01:00:46,510 --> 01:00:49,540
运行这个单元格，我们得到预期的输出。
Running the cell, we get the expected output.

596
01:00:50,414 --> 01:00:53,700
太棒了！现在你知道如何在 Python 中做决策了。
Awesome! Now you know how to make decisions in Python.

597
01:00:54,542 --> 01:00:57,924
我们从布尔值开始，用来表示是或否的答案。
We started with Booleans to represent yes or no answers.

598
01:00:58,766 --> 01:01:03,972
然后我们使用比较运算符来提问并自动获取这些答案。
Then we used comparison operators to ask questions and get those answers automatically.

599
01:01:04,878 --> 01:01:11,300
最后，我们用 if 和 else 语句将它们结合起来，根据这些答案运行不同的代码。
Finally, we brought it all together with if and else statements to run different code based on those answers.

600
01:01:12,046 --> 01:01:21,568
