1286
02:09:56,462 --> 02:09:58,436
好的，我们取得了不错的进展。
Okay, we've made good progress.

1287
02:09:59,374 --> 02:10:03,556
使用 zip 让我们的循环能够同时遍历两个列表。
Using zip allowed our loop to walk over two lists at the same time.

1288
02:10:04,464 --> 02:10:11,716
但为了在姓名和成绩之间用破折号格式化报告，我们需要它们作为两个独立的变量。
But to format our report with a dash in between the name and the grade, we need them both as separate variables.

1289
02:10:12,590 --> 02:10:20,292
我们可以通过手动索引从元组中把它们提取出来，用 pair 0 代表姓名，pair 1 代表分数。
We could pull them out of the tuple by indexing it ourselves, with pair 0 for the name and pair 1 for the score.

1290
02:10:21,166 --> 02:10:27,044
运行代码，它确实可行，但手动索引会让我们的循环变得有点难读。
Running the code, it works, but indexing manually makes our loop a bit harder to read.

1291
02:10:27,886 --> 02:10:36,292
如果有人重新审视这段代码，就得去查循环头，才能确认 x0 包含的是学生姓名而不是成绩。
Someone taking a fresh look at this code would have to refer back to the loop header to see that x0 contains a student name and not a grade.

1292
02:10:37,166 --> 02:10:43,236
只有在那里我们才能看到，在 zip 中学生排在第一位，所以 x0 一定代表一个学生。
Only there can we see that students are first in zip, so x0 must represent a student.

1293
02:10:44,144 --> 02:10:45,444
这不够直观。
Not very transparent.

1294
02:10:46,350 --> 02:10:53,444
为了提高循环的可读性，Python 允许我们在循环头中直接将元组的值分配给独立的变量。
To improve the readability of our loop, Python lets us assign the tuple's values to separate variables directly in the header.

1295
02:10:54,350 --> 02:11:01,476
为了拆分这个元组，我们将 x 替换为两个由逗号分隔的变量：student 和 score。
To split the tuple, we replace x with two variables, student and score, separated by a comma.

1296
02:11:02,382 --> 02:11:05,700
用这个循环头，zip 函数生成的仍然是一个元组。
With this header, the zip function still produces a tuple.

1297
02:11:06,350 --> 02:11:09,380
比如，一个包含 Alice 和 85 的元组。
For example, one with Alice and 85.

1298
02:11:10,414 --> 02:11:14,436
但现在，这个元组被拆分成了两个独立的变量。
But now, that tuple is pulled apart into two separate variables.

1299
02:11:15,438 --> 02:11:20,452
在 Python 中，将元组拆分到不同的变量中被称为元组解包。
In Python, splitting a tuple into separate variables is called tuple unpacking.

1300
02:11:21,486 --> 02:11:27,620
一旦它们在循环头中被赋值，我们就可以像使用任何其他变量一样，在循环体中使用这两个变量。
Once they've been assigned in the header, we can use these two variables in the loop body just like any other variable.

1301
02:11:28,910 --> 02:11:32,484
运行代码，我们就能打印出每个学生的名字及其对应的分数。
Running the code, we get each student's name printed with their score.

1302
02:11:33,518 --> 02:11:33,904
漂亮！
Nice!

1303
02:11:34,286 --> 02:11:39,780
解包为名字和分数分别提供了自己的变量，这样我们终于能打印报告了。
Unpacking gave the name and score their own variables, so we could finally print our report.

1304
02:11:40,782 --> 02:11:46,624
现在，包含姓名和成绩的报告对老师很有用，但学生想知道他们实际获得的等级。
Now, a report with names and grades is useful for a teacher, but students want to know their actual letter

1305
02:11:46,624 --> 02:11:52,356
我们可以用 zip 把包含字母等级的第三个列表与另外两个列表配对吗？
grade. Can we use zip to pair a third list containing letter grades with the other two?

1306
02:11:53,230 --> 02:11:54,340
答案是肯定的。
The answer is yes.

1307
02:11:54,606 --> 02:11:57,252
zip 函数可以配对任意数量的列表。
The zip function can pair any number of lists.

1308
02:11:58,126 --> 02:12:02,916
要添加第三个列表，我们只需在 zip 函数中将其作为另一个参数传入。
To add the third list, we simply pass it as another argument in the zip function.

1309
02:12:03,918 --> 02:12:07,588
现在，由 zip 生成的每个元组都将包含三个值。
Now each tuple generated by zip will hold three values.

1310
02:12:08,558 --> 02:12:12,196
为了获取这个第三个值，我们增加第三个循环变量。
To capture this third value, we add a third loop variable.

1311
02:12:13,198 --> 02:12:16,740
最后，我们可以在循环体中输出这个变量。
Finally, we can output this variable in the loop body.

1312
02:12:17,614 --> 02:12:23,940
运行代码，我们得到了每个学生的名字、分数和字母等级，而且全部匹配正确。
Running the code, we get each student's name, score, and a letter grade, all matched up.

1313
02:12:24,878 --> 02:12:29,252
当所有列表的元素数量都相同时，这种配对方式非常完美。
This pairing works perfectly when all of the lists have the same number of elements.

1314
02:12:30,144 --> 02:12:31,556
但有时它们并不相等。
But sometimes they don't.

1315
02:12:32,494 --> 02:12:39,844
假设 Bob 缺考了，所以 students 仍有三个元素，但 scores 和 grades 只有两个。
Suppose Bob missed the test, so students still has three elements, but scores and grades only have two.

1316
02:12:40,864 --> 02:12:43,460
运行代码，我们只得到了两对数据。
Running the code, we only get two pairs.

1317
02:12:44,302 --> 02:12:49,476
这是因为 zip 一旦到达最短列表的末尾就会停止创建配对。
That's because zip stops creating pairs the moment it reaches the end of the shortest list.

1318
02:12:50,144 --> 02:12:52,388
在这里，包括 scores 和 grades。
Here, both scores and grades.

1319
02:12:53,262 --> 02:12:57,988
仔细看，尽管 Bob 没有参加考试，但他还是被分配了一个分数。
Looking a bit closer, Bob was assigned a score even though he didn't take the test.

1320
02:12:58,830 --> 02:13:02,820
这是因为 zip 是纯粹根据位置来匹配项的。
This happened because zip matches items purely by position.

1321
02:13:03,264 --> 02:13:06,436
它根本不知道哪些内容真正属于一起。
It has no idea which ones truly belong together.

1322
02:13:07,374 --> 02:13:12,964
最糟糕的是，Python 既没有报错，也没有对这两个问题发出任何警告。
Worst of all, Python didn't raise an error or give us any warning about either of these issues.

1323
02:13:13,806 --> 02:13:20,548
所以这里的教训是：当你合并多个必须保持同步的列表时，需要格外小心。
So the lesson here is: when you're zipping several lists that all have to stay in sync, you need to be careful.

1324
02:13:21,550 --> 02:13:26,180
如果你可以更改数据的存储方式，这里用字典可能会更安全。
If you can change how the data is stored, it would probably be safer to use a dictionary here.

1325
02:13:27,182 --> 02:13:31,524
