1345
02:15:15,086 --> 02:15:23,204
这正是我们要做的，我们将一步步完成它，利用 Python 处理列表最方便的两个工具：enumerate
That's exactly what we're going to build, one step at a time, using two of Python's handiest tools for working with lists, enumerate

1346
02:15:23,470 --> 02:15:24,164
和 zip。
and zip.

1347
02:15:25,006 --> 02:15:30,564
如果你尝试了我们 enumerate 或 zip 视频中的练习笔记本，可以在我们讲解时检查你的进度。
If you tried the practice notebook from our enumerate or zip videos, you can check your work as we go.

1348
02:15:31,374 --> 02:15:34,724
如果你还没试过，我们在描述栏里提供了我们正在使用的笔记本链接。
And if you haven't, we link the notebook we're using in the description.

1349
02:15:35,598 --> 02:15:37,476
好了，让我们进入代码环节。
Okay, let's dive into the code.

1350
02:15:38,318 --> 02:15:45,572
作为构建最终曲目列表的第一步，让我们先输出 titles 列表中的所有歌曲名称及其对应的编号位置。
As a first step to our final track list, let's output all the song names in the titles list and their numbered positions.

1351
02:15:46,446 --> 02:15:50,372
要显示这些标题，我们只需遍历 titles 列表。
To display these titles, we simply loop over the titles list.

1352
02:15:51,214 --> 02:15:54,308
但这没法让我们获取到项目的序号。
But that doesn't give us access to the item's positions.

1353
02:15:55,278 --> 02:16:00,932
为了获取这些数字，我们在循环头里用 enumerate 函数包裹 titles 列表。
To get those numbers, we wrap the titles list in the enumerate function right in the loop header.

1354
02:16:01,774 --> 02:16:08,516
现在，在循环的每一次迭代中，enumerate 函数都会生成一个包含位置和标题的元组。
Now, on each iteration of the loop, the enumerate function generates a tuple containing the position and the title.

1355
02:16:09,422 --> 02:16:17,264
为了同时获取这两个值并在循环体中独立使用，我们将它们解包到两个变量 number
To capture both these values and use them independently in the loop body, we unpack them into two variables number

1356
02:16:17,614 --> 02:16:18,308
和 title 中。
and title.

1357
02:16:19,182 --> 02:16:23,332
在循环主体内，我们可以用 F string 来打印这些变量。
Inside the body of the loop, we can print those variables using an F string.

1358
02:16:24,238 --> 02:16:28,004
如果 F strings 对你来说是新概念，描述栏里有相关的视频链接。
If F strings are new to you, there's a video on them linked in the description.

1359
02:16:28,974 --> 02:16:33,540
在 F string 里面，我们将打印数字、一个点，然后是标题。
Inside the F string, we'll print the number, a dot, and then the title.

1360
02:16:34,446 --> 02:16:38,308
运行代码后，我们的输出结果已经接近预期了。
If we run the code, our output is close to what we want.

1361
02:16:39,150 --> 02:16:43,748
但由于 enumerate 函数的默认行为，这些数字是从零开始的。
But the numbers start from zero, since that's the default behavior of the enumerate function.

1362
02:16:44,750 --> 02:16:50,596
为了改变这一点，我们可以给 enumerate 函数传递 start 等于 1 的参数。
To change this, we can pass the argument start equals 1 to the enumerate function.

1363
02:16:51,502 --> 02:16:56,740
再次运行代码，我们的四首歌就会清晰地按 1 到 4 进行编号。
Running the code again, our four songs come out cleanly numbered 1 through 4.

1364
02:16:57,616 --> 02:17:00,964
好了，这是我们最终目标输出的一个很好的开端。
Okay, that's a good start on the final output we're building towards.

1365
02:17:01,998 --> 02:17:04,196
接下来，我们要加上每首歌的时长。
Next, we'll add each song's duration.

1366
02:17:05,102 --> 02:17:10,596
这些长度提供在另一个叫 durations 的列表中，并且与标题列表一一对应。
Those lengths are given to us in a second list called durations, lined up with their titles list.

1367
02:17:11,468 --> 02:17:17,124
为了同时遍历这两个列表，我们在 enumerate 调用内部直接调用 zip 函数。
To loop through both lists together, we hand them to the zip function right inside the enumerate call.

1368
02:17:17,998 --> 02:17:20,740
没错，你可以嵌套这些函数。
And yes, you can nest these functions.

1369
02:17:21,614 --> 02:17:27,780
enumerate 可以顺利处理我们提供的任何序列，而 zip 的结果就是一个元组序列。
Enumerate happily works on any sequence we give it, and the result of zip is just a sequence of tuples.

1370
02:17:28,750 --> 02:17:35,296
Zip 根据位置将列表项配对，所以现在 enumerate 在每次循环中都会给我们一个数字和一个配对。
Zip pairs list items by position, so now enumerate hands us a number and a pair on each pass.

1371
02:17:36,174 --> 02:17:39,332
这意味着我们需要把这些数据拆成两层来解包。
That means we need to unpack that data in two layers.

1372
02:17:40,254 --> 02:17:43,204
首先是 enumerate 函数生成的数字，
First, the number produced by the enumerate function,

1373
02:17:44,174 --> 02:17:48,388
然后是从元组内部提取出的标题和时长。
then the title and duration from inside the tuple.

1374
02:17:49,262 --> 02:17:55,012
一旦解包完成，我们就可以在循环体里像使用普通变量一样使用所有这些内容。
Once unpacked, though, we can use all these just like any other regular variable in the loop body.

1375
02:17:55,886 --> 02:18:00,611
所以为了在打印输出中包含时长，我们只需把它加到 F string 里。
So to include the duration in the printed output, we simply add it to the F string.

1376
02:18:01,486 --> 02:18:06,340
运行代码，现在每首歌都会在编号旁边显示它的长度。
Running the code, every song now shows its length right next to its number.

1377
02:18:07,150 --> 02:18:09,508
太棒了！这四首主要歌曲搞定了。
Great! That's the main four songs done.

1378
02:18:10,350 --> 02:18:13,700
但我们构建的完整曲目列表还有三个额外的奖励曲目。
But the full track list we're building has three more bonus tracks.

1379
02:18:14,700 --> 02:18:20,495
这些奖励曲目在它们各自的两个列表中：bonus titles 和 bonus durations。
These bonus tracks are waiting in their own two lists, bonus titles and bonus durations.

1380
02:18:21,422 --> 02:18:30,020
我们想把它们打印在曲目列表的末尾，编号要接续之前的计数，也就是 5、6 和 7，而不是重新从 1 开始。
We want to print them at the end of the track list, numbered to continue the count, 5, 6, and 7, rather than starting over at 1.

1381
02:18:30,861 --> 02:18:36,932
要做到这一点，我们可以重用刚刚写好的那个循环，只是把目标指向奖励曲目列表即可。
To do this, we can reuse the loop we just wrote, just pointed at the bonus lists instead.

1382
02:18:37,772 --> 02:18:41,316
唯一的其他变化是 enumerate 编号的起始位置。
The only other change is where the enumerate numbering begins.

1383
02:18:42,156 --> 02:18:46,884
enumerate 函数的 start 参数可以是任何我们想要的数字，而不只是 1。
The enumerate function's start argument can be any number we like, not just one.

1384
02:18:47,726 --> 02:18:54,500
因为主专辑到第 4 首曲目就结束了，所以我们将 start 设置为 5 而不是 1。
Since the main album ends at track 4, we pass start equals 5 instead of start equals 1.

1385
02:18:55,534 --> 02:19:03,780
然后为了区分这两个部分，我们在每个部分上方打印一个标题，在第一个循环前写主专辑，在第二个循环前写奖励曲目。
Then to keep the two sections distinct, we print a heading above each, main album before the first loop, and bonus tracks before the second.

1386
02:19:04,718 --> 02:19:10,628
运行代码后，奖励曲目现在会显示在它们自己的标题下，编号为 5 到 7。
Running the code, the bonus tracks now slot in under their own heading, numbered 5 through 7.

1387
02:19:11,468 --> 02:19:15,044
太棒了！我们现在有了一个格式整齐的最终曲目列表。
Awesome! We now have our finished track list nicely formatted.

1388
02:19:15,950 --> 02:19:23,843
enumerate 函数提供了编号，zip 函数把我们的两个列表配对在一起，而结合这两者让我们能同时完成这两项操作。
The enumerate function gave us the numbering, the zip function paired our lists together, and combining the two let us do both at once.

1389
02:19:24,816 --> 02:19:35,616
到目前为止，我们已经非常熟悉使用 for循环来遍历数据集合了。而且正如我们所见，其中两个集合——列表和元组——是按位置存储数据的。
By now we're very familiar using for loops to iterate through collections of data. And as we've seen, two of those collections, lists and tuples, store data by position.

1390
02:19:36,016 --> 02:19:39,108
但是按位置存储数据有一些局限性。
But storing data by position has some limitations.

1391
02:19:39,376 --> 02:19:45,636
在下一个部分，我们将看到一种新型数据，它允许我们创建自定义标签来存储数据。
In the next section, we'll see a new type of data that allows us to create custom labels to store our data with.

1392
02:19:46,415 --> 02:19:51,140
如果我告诉你有一种 Python 数据结构可以像真正的字典一样工作呢？
What if I told you there's a Python data structure that works like a real dictionary?

1393
02:19:52,014 --> 02:19:56,548
当你查找一个词或一个键时，你会得到它的定义或值。
When you look up a word or a key, you get its definition or value.

1394
02:19:57,390 --> 02:20:04,004
当你想要用有意义的标签来组织数据时，比如好友的电子邮箱地址，这非常有用。
That's pretty useful when you want to organize data with meaningful labels, such as the email addresses of your best friends.

1395
02:20:05,006 --> 02:20:07,936
这种数据结构被称为 Python 字典。
This data structure is called a Python dictionary.

1396
02:20:08,174 --> 02:20:09,636
让我们看看如何创建一个。
Let's see how to create one.

1397
02:20:10,510 --> 02:20:14,244
要创建一个 Python 字典，我们从花括号开始。
To create a Python dictionary, we start with curly brackets.

1398
02:20:15,182 --> 02:20:18,628
在这些括号之间，我们写入字典条目。
In between those brackets, we write the dictionary entries.

1399
02:20:19,470 --> 02:20:22,980
首先让我们创建一个条目来存储 Bob 的电子邮箱地址。
Let's first create an entry to store Bob's email address.

1400
02:20:23,918 --> 02:20:28,420
每个字典条目都有两个部分：一个键和一个值。
Each dictionary entry has two parts, a key and a value.

1401
02:20:29,326 --> 02:20:33,220
键是我们想要用来访问值的标签。
The key is the label we want to use to access the value.

1402
02:20:34,190 --> 02:20:39,108
在 Bob 的例子中，键是他的名字，而值是他的电子邮箱地址。
In Bob's case, the key is his name and the value is his email address.

1403
02:20:40,110 --> 02:20:45,508
在 Python 中，连接键和值的语法是冒号。
In Python, the syntax we use to connect the key and the value is a colon.

1404
02:20:46,446 --> 02:20:53,188
这类条目被称为键值对，因为每个键都链接到一个特定的值。
Entries like this are called key value pairs because each key is linked to a specific value.

1405
02:20:54,190 --> 02:20:58,496
当字典有多个条目时，我们用逗号将它们隔开。
When a dictionary has multiple entries, we separate them with commas.

1406
02:20:59,374 --> 02:21:03,812
然后我们可以同样地为我们的其他朋友创建键值对。
We can then similarly create key value pairs for our other friends.

1407
02:21:07,630 --> 02:21:11,140
就这样，你就创建了你的第一个 Python 字典。
And just like that, you've created your first Python dictionary.

1408
02:21:12,110 --> 02:21:16,132
现在，让我们看看查询 Bob 的电子邮箱地址有多快。
Now, let's see how quickly we can look up Bob's email address.

1409
02:21:17,102 --> 02:21:22,256
为了做到这一点，我们先将这个字典赋值给变量 contacts。
To do this, let's first assign our dictionary to the variable contacts.

1410
02:21:23,374 --> 02:21:29,860
要从字典中获取 Bob 的电子邮箱地址，我们在字典名称后面加上方括号。
To retrieve Bob's email address from the dictionary, we follow the name of our dictionary with square brackets.

1411
02:21:30,798 --> 02:21:36,612
在这些括号里，我们放入要查找的键，也就是带引号的 Bob。
Inside those brackets, we put the key we're looking for, in this case, Bob in quotes.

1412
02:21:37,582 --> 02:21:43,556
当我们运行这段代码时，会得到 Bob 的邮箱地址：ilovebunnies at gmail.com。
And when we run this, we get Bob's email address, ilovebunnies at gmail.com.

1413
02:21:44,526 --> 02:21:51,428
换句话说，通过使用键 Bob，我们可以直接获取字典中对应的对应的值。
In other words, by using the key Bob, we can directly access the corresponding value in the dictionary.

1414
02:21:52,398 --> 02:21:57,636
太棒了！现在你知道如何创建字典以及如何使用键来获取值了。
Awesome! Now you know how to create dictionaries and access values using keys.

1415
02:21:58,606 --> 02:22:04,420
但正如你可能知道的，在 Python 中，字典并不是组织物品集合的唯一方式。
But as you might know, dictionaries are not the only way we can organize collections of items in Python.

1416
02:22:05,358 --> 02:22:12,292
例如，我们不一定要创建一个包含朋友邮箱的字典，也可以创建一个邮箱列表。
For example, instead of creating a dictionary of our friends' emails, we could have created a list of emails.

1417
02:22:14,510 --> 02:22:16,580
使用列表会不会是更好的主意呢？
Would using a list be a better idea?

1418
02:22:17,550 --> 02:22:23,492
在继续之前，如果你需要复习一下关于 Python 列表的知识，我们在简介里放了一个链接。
Before we go any further, if you need to refresh your knowledge of Python lists, we've left a link in the description.

1419
02:22:24,398 --> 02:22:30,852
现在，我们来讨论一下为什么在当前的例子中，使用字典而不是列表是更好的选择。
Now, let's discuss why using a dictionary instead of a list is a better idea in the current example.

1420
02:22:31,694 --> 02:22:37,828
在我们的例子中，列表和字典包含的都是相同的值，也就是我们朋友的邮箱。
In our example, both the list and dictionary contain the same values, our friends' emails.

1421
02:22:38,798 --> 02:22:42,372
但区别在于如何识别这些值。
But the difference is how the values are identified.

1422
02:22:43,342 --> 02:22:49,252
在列表中，项目是根据它们在列表中的位置来标识或索引的。
In a list, the items are identified or indexed by their position in the list.

1423
02:22:50,222 --> 02:22:56,388
如果我们想获取 Bob 的邮箱地址，我们需要记住它是列表中的第一个项目
If we want to get Bob's email address, we need to remember that it is the first item in the list

1424
02:22:57,358 --> 02:22:59,428
并用零来索引这个列表。
and index that list with zero.

1425
02:23:00,398 --> 02:23:03,460
如果我们的联系人列表里只有三个朋友，这样做是合理的。
That's reasonable with three friends in our contact list.

1426
02:23:03,856 --> 02:23:11,524
但如果你非常受欢迎，有几十个朋友，要记住每个朋友邮箱在列表中的位置就会变得非常困难。
But if you're really popular and have dozens of friends, remembering the position of each friend's email in the list will be very hard.

1427
02:23:12,558 --> 02:23:17,476
而使用字典时，我们只需要记住朋友的名字就能获取到他们的邮箱。
With a dictionary, we only need to remember our friends' names to get their emails.

1428
02:23:18,446 --> 02:23:19,696
核心点就在这里。
Here's the bottom line.

1429
02:23:20,078 --> 02:23:25,604
对于那些带有明确标签的数据，使用字典会让操作变得更简单、更直观。
Dictionaries make it more simple and intuitive to work with data that have meaningful labels.

1430
02:23:26,446 --> 02:23:34,500
例如，它们非常适合用来组织用户名和密码、产品及其价格，或者学生及其成绩等信息。
For example, they're great for organizing things like usernames and passwords, products and their prices, or students and their grades.

1431
02:23:35,406 --> 02:23:41,892
在每种情况下，键都充当了一个清晰的标签，帮助我们快速获取相关的值。
In each case, the key serves as a clear label that helps us quickly access the related value.

1432
02:23:42,862 --> 02:23:43,376
太棒了！
Awesome!

1433
02:23:43,630 --> 02:23:51,140
到目前为止，你已经理解了字典和列表之间的区别，并知道什么时候使用字典更好。
At this point, you understand the differences between dictionaries and lists and know when it is better to use a dictionary.

1434
02:23:52,206 --> 02:24:01,252
但为了在自己的项目中有效地使用字典，了解哪些类型的数据可以作为键和值非常重要。
But to use dictionaries effectively in your own projects, it is important to understand what kinds of data can be used as keys and values.

1435
02:24:02,286 --> 02:24:06,340
让我们深入研究一下关于键和值的规则以及最佳实践。
Let's dive into the rules and best practices for keys and values.

1436
02:24:07,278 --> 02:24:11,940
首先，字典的值可以是任何数据类型。
First, the values of a dictionary can be of any data type.

1437
02:24:12,750 --> 02:24:21,540
例如，我们可以创建一个“兄弟姐妹”字典，其中每个值都是一个表示每个朋友有多少个兄弟姐妹的整数。
For example, we could create a siblings dictionary where each value is an integer showing how many siblings each friend has.

1438
02:24:22,510 --> 02:24:31,396
或者我们可以创建一个“是否有宠物”字典，其中的值是布尔值：如果朋友有宠物就是 true，否则就是 false。
Or we could create a has pet dictionary where the values are Booleans, true if the friend has a pet and false if not.

1439
02:24:32,366 --> 02:24:37,540
注意在“是否有宠物”这个字典中，值 true 出现了多次。
Notice that in the has pet dictionary, the value true appears more than once.

1440
02:24:38,382 --> 02:24:39,780
这完全没问题。
That's totally fine.

1441
02:24:40,782 --> 02:24:44,388
在 Python 中，不同的键可以共享同一个值。
In Python, different keys can share the same value.

1442
02:24:45,230 --> 02:24:48,612
但是，字典的键必须是唯一的。
However, dictionary keys must be unique.

1443
02:24:49,486 --> 02:24:53,796
例如，我们试着为 Wendy 添加第二个邮箱地址。
For example, let's try to add a second email address for Wendy.

1444
02:24:54,766 --> 02:25:01,540
为此，我们在字典定义中写第二个 Wendy 键，并让它与第二个邮箱配对。
To do this, we'll write a second Wendy key in the dictionary definition and pair it with a second email.

1445
02:25:02,510 --> 02:25:09,476
当我们运行单元格并显示更新后的字典时，只有其中一个 Wendy 条目被添加到字典中。
When we run the cell and display our updated dictionary, only one of the entries for Wendy has been added to the dictionary.

1446
02:25:10,510 --> 02:25:13,316
仔细想想，这种行为是合理的。
If you think about it, this behavior makes sense.

1447
02:25:14,190 --> 02:25:20,164
如果我们的字典有两个 Wendy 键，Python 怎么知道该返回哪个邮箱呢？
If our dictionary had two Wendy keys, how would Python know which email to return?

1448
02:25:23,086 --> 02:25:26,980
最后，字典的键并不局限于字符串。
Finally, the keys of a dictionary aren't limited to strings.

1449
02:25:27,918 --> 02:25:31,296
它们可以是整数、浮点数，甚至是布尔值。
They can be integers, floats, or even booleans.

1450
02:25:32,206 --> 02:25:38,436
话虽如此，字符串是最常用的选择，所以在接下来的视频中我们将使用字符串。
That said, strings are by far the most common choice, so that's what we'll use in the rest of this video.

1451
02:25:39,406 --> 02:25:43,556
太棒了！现在你了解了字典键和值的规则。
Great! Now you understand the rules for dictionary keys and values.

1452
02:25:44,526 --> 02:25:53,252
这些信息足以创建字典了，但如果你想通过添加或移除条目来修改现有字典呢？
That's enough information to create dictionaries, but what if you want to modify an existing dictionary by adding or removing entries?

1453
02:25:54,158 --> 02:26:02,916
例如，假设我们交了一个叫 Alex 的新朋友，并想把他的邮箱 coolalex at gmail.com 添加到我们的字典中。
For example, let's say we've made a new friend named Alex and want to add their email, coolalex at gmail.com, to our dictionary.

1454
02:26:03,726 --> 02:26:04,932
这很容易做到。
That's easy to do.

1455
02:26:05,902 --> 02:26:12,548
只需写出字典名称，后面加上方括号，并在里面放入新键 Alex。
Simply write the dictionary name, followed by square brackets, with the new key Alex inside.

1456
02:26:13,550 --> 02:26:19,044
然后使用等号将 coolAlex at gmail.com 赋值为值。
